  "final_message": "I fixed the off-by-one bug in `paginate()`, and `python3 -m unittest -v test_public.py` now passes.\n\nThe bug was that the start index used `page * page_size`. Pages are numbered from 1, so page 1 skipped the first page of items. I changed it to `(page - 1) * page_size`, the same formula `page_bounds` already uses. `total_pages` and `page_bounds` are untouched.\n\nA quick check on `[1, 2, 3, 4, 5]` with 2 items per page: page 2 gives `[3, 4]`, page 3 gives `[5]`, and page 4 gives `[]`.\n\nDONE: Fixed the start index in paginate() to (page - 1) * page_size so pages are 1-indexed; public test passes.",
